  "text_md": "## Panteion University of Social & Political Sciences Department of Social Anthropology\n\n13.30 – 14. 30 Lunch Break\n# Programme 27th April\n\n9.30 – 10.00: Greetings and introduction to the workshop (*Athina Athanasiou*, Chair of Department of Social Anthropology, *Eleana Yalouri*, Director of the Laboratory for Anthropological Research\n\n|Director of the Laboratory for Anthropological Research||Kush|\n|---|---|---|\n|For the Organizers: Diana Riboli, ISARS President,|15.10 – 15.50 Lu Fangfang||\n|Lidia Guzy, University of Cork)||The Making of Shaman among the Three Northern Minorities in|\n\n## Session I\n\n*Chair: Lidia Guzy*\n\n10.00 – 10.40: *Stefano Beggiora*\n## The Khonds and the Jungle: A Case Study on Indigenous India\n\n10.40 – 11.20: *Davide Torri*\n## Sacred and Alive: Human, Non-human and Landscape in the\n\n## (Buddhist) Himalayas\n\n11.20 – 11.40 Coffee Break\n11.40 – 12.20 *Ivan Tacey*\n## Rearranging Cosmic Relations: Cosmopolitics in the Anthropocene\n\n12.20 -13.20 Discussion\n## Session II\n\n*Chair: Naran Bilik*\n\n14.30 – 15.10 *Taj Khan Kalash*\n## Ecological Living in Peril: The Case of Kalasha Society in Hindu\n\n## Kush\n\n## China and the Hero’s Theme\n\n15.50 – 16.30 *Ranju Hasini Sahoo*\n## Amarkantak: The Eco Cosmology and Sacred Complex\n\n16.30 – 17.30 Discussion\n**28th April**\n\n## Session I\n\n*Chair: Stefano Beggiora*\n\n10.00– 10.40: *Naran Bilik*\n## Unblocking the Blockage between Earth and Heaven: Shamanism as Cultural Intimacy in China\n",
